Package: arbor
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: see where your disk space grows
 Arbor is a disk usage analyzer for Linux: it scans folders asynchronously
 and presents sizes, item counts and modification dates as a sortable tree
 plus rings and treemap visualizations. Items can be opened with the default
 handler, their path copied, and moved to the Trash — always behind a
 mandatory confirmation dialog with an undo.
 .
 This is an independent, clean-room implementation of the behavior of GNOME
 Baobab 50.0, built from a black-box behavioral specification; it contains no
 upstream code.
